# tasks_flush_on_suspend: rvg_device_finish_suspend flushes every task, in-process or in its service, before it writes the blob (section 4.7), but the flush, like a synchronize, copies out only resources that needsSync (guest-invalid and host-valid). A private buffer filled under an exec without the invalidate-guest flag is not one: in-process the guest page keeps its old bytes through rvg_device_finish_suspend. In the service the fill landed at once (a Shared detach buffer). suspend_writeback locks the flush that does copy. The blob reports the host (device info), so the expected file is keyed by it.
